<section class="hero">
  <h1>Pavel Bushuyeu</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    I am a graduate AI researcher at the
    <a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu">University of Hawaiʻi at Mānoa</a>,
    in the department of
    <a href="http://ics.hawaii.edu/">Information and Computer Sciences</a>.
    I work on vision-language-action models for humanoid locomotion and
    manipulation in
    <a href="https://igormolybog.github.io">Prof. Igor Molybog’s lab</a>, and on
    clinical foundation models for the population of Hawaiʻi.
  </p>

  <p class="muted">
    Before graduate school I spent nine years building data-heavy B2B products
    in fintech, infrastructure monitoring, and video — work that still shapes
    how I think about evaluation, data quality, and what makes a model useful
    outside a benchmark. <a href="/research/">More on my research</a>, or
    <a href="/experience/">the full record</a>.
  </p>

  <ul class="inline-links">
    {%- for link in site.links %}
